  "measure_key": "autumn_budget_2024__employer_nics_package",
  "notes": "PE represents the employer rate and weekly secondary threshold (\u00a396 \u00d7 52 = \u00a34,992 in the installed model). It has no Employment Allowance or firm entity, so the allowance increase and \u00a3100,000 test removal are missing. policyengine_uk/parameters/gov/contrib/policyengine/employer_ni/employee_incidence.yaml sets gov.contrib.policyengine.employer_ni.employee_incidence to 1, and policyengine_uk/variables/contrib/policyengine/employer_ni/employer_ni_fixed_employer_cost_change.py adjusts wages holding employer cost fixed. The resulting wage change moves employee-side Income Tax and NICs, which is why the PE Income-tax head is non-zero.",
